Subject: [PATCH] mega_moe: single kernel GEMM2 pipelining and 256-column GEMM1 units

- GEMM2: the 9 K-tiles are fully unrolled; the W2 tile of K-tile k+1 is issued in 16-column groups right after
  the MFMA group that frees its registers (no extra VGPRs); weight base addresses go through readfirstlane so
  the buffer descriptors are uniform (no waterfall loops); the tile metadata and first W2 loads are issued
  before waiting for the m-tile's GEMM1-ready flag (GEMM1 output is still read only after the flag and the L1
  invalidate).
- GEMM1: buckets of >= 256 tokens per rank use tile_n 256 (18 work units per m-tile instead of 36); the XCD split
  boundaries are aligned so each 256-byte scale block is still written by one XCD.
- DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, EP8, 384 tokens/rank, captured decode routing: 372 -> 349 us per call; outputs
  bit-identical to the unpatched kernel on uniform, zipf and captured routing. Cost: 28 VGPR and 16 SGPR
  spills (outside the K-loop). The DeepSeek-V4-Pro shape was not measured.

Base: amd-aiter 0.1.29 + 0001 + 0002.
